@startuml class
!include style.puml
!pragma layout smetana

title Color Manager - Domain Class Diagram
left to right direction
hide circle

class User <<entity>> {
  {field} ID : INT {PK, auto increment}
  {field} FirstName : VARCHAR(50)
  {field} LastName : VARCHAR(50)
  {field} Login : VARCHAR(50)
  {field} Password : VARCHAR(50)
}

class Color <<entity>> {
  {field} ID : INT {PK, auto increment}
  {field} Name : VARCHAR(50)
  {field} UserID : INT
}

User "0..1" -- "0..*" Color : owns\nID = UserID

note top of User
  User maps to COP4331.Users.
  Color maps to COP4331.Colors.
  These are domain entities; the PHP
  endpoints use procedural functions.
end note

note bottom of Color
  UserID is a logical reference to Users.ID.
  No FOREIGN KEY constraint is declared,
  so a Color may have no matching User.
end note

legend bottom
  All fields are NOT NULL.
  Text fields default to ''; UserID defaults to 0.
  PK = primary key.
endlegend

@enduml
